            <body>Source: ah5-core-java-spring/consumer-authorization/documentation/v5.3.0/ConsumerAuthorization-v5.3.0-authorizationManagement-HTTP-IDD.tex; The service is registered in the ServiceRegistry with the interface template generic_https (generic_http when TLS is disabled), access port 8445 and base path /consumerauthorization/authorization/mgmt. The operations property of the interface lists the operations below with their method and path relative to the base path (path parameters are placeholders such as \texttt{{id}} that the consumer fills in):

\noindent\begin{longtable}{| p{5.2cm} | p{1.6cm} | p{8.4cm} |} \hline
\rowcolor{gray!33} Operation &amp; Method &amp; Path \\ \hline \endhead
grant-policies &amp; POST &amp; /grant \\ \hline
revoke-policies &amp; DELETE &amp; /revoke \\ \hline
query-policies &amp; POST &amp; /query \\ \hline
check-policies &amp; POST &amp; /check \\ \hline
\end{longtable}

\newpage</body>
