            <body>Source: ah5-core-java-spring/consumer-authorization/documentation/v5.3.0/ConsumerAuthorization-v5.3.0-generalManagement-HTTP-IDD.tex; The service is registered in the ServiceRegistry with the interface template generic_https (generic_http when TLS is disabled), access port 8445 and base path /consumerauthorization/general/mgmt. The operations property of the interface lists the operations below with their method and path relative to the base path (path parameters are placeholders such as \texttt{{id}} that the consumer fills in):

\noindent\begin{longtable}{| p{5.2cm} | p{1.6cm} | p{8.4cm} |} \hline
\rowcolor{gray!33} Operation &amp; Method &amp; Path \\ \hline \endhead
get-log &amp; POST &amp; /logs \\ \hline
get-config &amp; GET &amp; /get-config \\ \hline
\end{longtable}

\newpage</body>
