        <packagedElement xmi:id="_ah53_9bbdd869a8714ddef435e966" name="blacklistDiscovery_SD" xmi:type="uml:Class" />
        <packagedElement xmi:id="_ah53_c0fb352708daa30c60833cc3" name="blacklistDiscovery_HTTP_IDD" xmi:type="uml:Class">
          <generalization xmi:id="_ah53_62b579b0d8668a1e96cc10f3" general="_ah53_9bbdd869a8714ddef435e966" xmi:type="uml:Generalization" />
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_ah53_6bbe8bdd1899cca69777c15a" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <body>Source: ah5-Blacklist-java-spring/documentation/v5.3.0/Blacklist-v5.3.0-blacklistDiscovery-HTTP-IDD.tex; The service is registered in the ServiceRegistry with the interface template generic_https, policy CERT_AUTH, access address blacklist, port 8464 and base path /blacklist. The operations property of the interface lists the operations below with their method and path relative to the base path (path parameters are placeholders such as \texttt{{id}} that the consumer fills in):

\noindent\begin{longtable}{| p{5.2cm} | p{1.6cm} | p{8.4cm} |} \hline
\rowcolor{gray!33} Operation &amp; Method &amp; Path \\ \hline \endhead
check &amp; GET &amp; \texttt{/check/{systemName}} \\ \hline
lookup &amp; GET &amp; /lookup \\ \hline
\end{longtable}

\newpage</body>
          </ownedComment>
