        <packagedElement xmi:id="_ah53_5ba89932bbbd3c635f84b91c" name="dataProxy_SD" xmi:type="uml:Class" />
        <packagedElement xmi:id="_ah53_ad38279124edb3e867e5e2fc" name="dataProxy_HTTP_IDD" xmi:type="uml:Class">
          <generalization xmi:id="_ah53_dd70e16c9b52b06d12d99748" general="_ah53_5ba89932bbbd3c635f84b91c" xmi:type="uml:Generalization" />
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_ah53_30bc5d14ca3c14dc7be46fe7" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <body>Source: ah5-DataManager-java-spring/documentation/v5.3.0/DataManager-v5.3.0-dataProxy-HTTP-IDD.tex; The service is registered in the ServiceRegistry with the interface template generic_https, policy CERT_AUTH, access address datamanager, port 8461 and base path /datamanager/data-proxy. The operations property of the interface lists the operations below with their method and path relative to the base path (path parameters are placeholders such as \texttt{{id}} that the consumer fills in):

\noindent\begin{longtable}{| p{5.2cm} | p{1.6cm} | p{8.4cm} |} \hline
\rowcolor{gray!33} Operation &amp; Method &amp; Path \\ \hline \endhead
list-systems &amp; GET &amp; /systems \\ \hline
list-services &amp; GET &amp; \texttt{/systems/{systemName}/services} \\ \hline
get-data &amp; GET &amp; \texttt{/systems/{systemName}/services/{serviceName}/data} \\ \hline
put-data &amp; PUT &amp; \texttt{/systems/{systemName}/services/{serviceName}/data} \\ \hline
\end{longtable}

\newpage</body>
          </ownedComment>
