        <packagedElement xmi:id="_ah53_94fba89e94c89cf8cac18794" name="gateTunnelConnection_HTTP_IDD" xmi:type="uml:Class">
          <generalization xmi:id="_ah53_f2e2f98b5fe20f64cc6c3f05" general="_ah53_7aecfc988890cc8e1bb8586b" xmi:type="uml:Generalization" />
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_ah53_3c11838dc85899ac26b60377" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <body>Source: ah5-GateTunnel-java-spring/documentation/v5.3.0/GateTunnel-v5.3.0-gateTunnelConnection-HTTP-IDD.tex; The service is registered in the ServiceRegistry with the interface template generic_https, policy CERT_AUTH, access address gatetunnel, port 8453 and base path /gatetunnel. The operations property of the interface lists the operations below with their method and path relative to the base path (path parameters are placeholders such as \texttt{{id}} that the consumer fills in):

\noindent\begin{longtable}{| p{5.2cm} | p{1.6cm} | p{8.4cm} |} \hline
\rowcolor{gray!33} Operation &amp; Method &amp; Path \\ \hline \endhead
connect-provider &amp; POST &amp; /connect_provider \\ \hline
connect-consumer &amp; POST &amp; /connect_consumer \\ \hline
close-sessions &amp; POST &amp; /close_sessions \\ \hline
open-provider-session &amp; POST &amp; /intercloud/provider \\ \hline
open-consumer-session &amp; POST &amp; /intercloud/consumer \\ \hline
\end{longtable}

\newpage</body>
          </ownedComment>
